{{!
    @template local_unifiedgrader/help_section_students

    Help page partial: what students see. Written to the student.

    Context variables:
    * img - object - Screenshot URLs keyed by file name in pix/help.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "img": {
            "friction_ready": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/friction_ready",
            "friction_timer": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/friction_timer",
            "student_assignment_page": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/student_assignment_page",
            "student_feedback_view": "https://moodle.example.com/theme/image.php/boost/local_unifiedgrader/1/help/student_feedback_view"
        }
    }
}}
<section id="students" class="local-unifiedgrader-help-part">
<header class="local-unifiedgrader-help-part-head">
    <p class="local-unifiedgrader-help-kicker"><i class="fa fa-graduation-cap" aria-hidden="true"></i> For students</p>
    <h2>Reading your feedback</h2>
    <p>Where to find your grade and feedback, and what each part of the feedback page means.
    Teachers: this is what your students see.</p>
</header>

{{! ----- Reading feedback ----- }}
<section id="student-feedback">
<h3>Find and read your feedback</h3>

<ol class="local-unifiedgrader-help-steps">
    <li><strong>Open the activity.</strong> When your teacher has posted your grade, a banner
        appears near the top of the assignment, quiz, forum or BigBlueButton page.</li>
    <li><strong>Press the button in the banner.</strong> On an assignment it reads
        <strong>View Annotated Feedback</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Read the feedback page.</strong> It shows your work with your teacher's marks, their comments, and your grade.</li>
</ol>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
    <a href="{{img.student_assignment_page}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.student_assignment_page}}" width="1300" height="874" loading="lazy"
             alt="A student's assignment page. A banner under the due date reads View Annotated Feedback, with a button of the same name on its right. The submission status table follows.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>The <strong>View Annotated Feedback</strong> banner on your assignment page.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h4>What is on the feedback page</h4>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Your document</strong> with highlights, ticks, crosses and other marks.</li>
    <li><strong>Margin comments.</strong> Each numbered pin on the page has a card beside it with your teacher's comment.</li>
    <li><strong>Overall feedback</strong> on the right, and the rubric or marking guide if one was used.</li>
    <li><strong>Your grade</strong> at the top right.</li>
    <li><strong>Download feedback PDF</strong>: a copy of your document with the marks printed in, to keep.</li>
    <li>For a forum you see your posts; for a quiz, your attempt with the marker's comments; for a
        live session, the recording with comments at the moments they refer to.</li>
</ul>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
    <a href="{{img.student_feedback_view}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.student_feedback_view}}" width="1300" height="874" loading="lazy"
             alt="The feedback page: an essay with coloured highlights and a numbered pin linked to a comment card in the margin, the Overall Feedback text on the right, a Download feedback PDF button, and Grade: 68 / 100 (68%) at the top right.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>The feedback page: your marked document, a margin comment, overall feedback,
    your grade and <strong>Download feedback PDF</strong>.</figcaption>
</figure>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-note">
    <p><strong>No banner yet?</strong> Your teacher has not posted your grade. Marking may be
    finished for some students and not others, and grades are sometimes posted on a set date.</p>
</div>
</section>

{{! ----- Friction walk ----- }}
<section id="student-friction">
<h3>The feedback walk (Friction Feedback)</h3>

<p>In some activities your mark appears only after you have read the feedback. This is called
Friction Feedback. It takes a minute or two.</p>

<ol class="local-unifiedgrader-help-steps">
    <li><strong>Open your feedback.</strong> A box appears over the page. It explains: <em>Read the
        feedback on this step. Your mark follows once you have seen each part.</em></li>
    <li><strong>Read the step.</strong> A counter shows where you are (<em>1 of 3</em>). Each step
        is one part of the feedback: a rubric criterion, a marked question, or the overall
        comment. A ring fills while you read.</li>
    <li><strong>Press <em>I have seen this</em></strong> when the ring is complete and the button appears.</li>
    <li><strong>See your mark.</strong> After the last step your grade, the points and the feedback PDF appear.</li>
</ol>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shots">
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.friction_timer}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.friction_timer}}" width="1300" height="874" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The Friction Feedback box over the feedback page: step 1 of 1, Overall feedback, with the teacher's comment and a partly filled timer ring.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>Reading a step. The ring is still filling.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.friction_ready}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.friction_ready}}" width="1300" height="874" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The same box with a green tick in place of the ring and an I have seen this button.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>The ring is complete: <strong>I have seen this</strong> is ready.</figcaption>
    </figure>
</div>

<ul>
    <li>The timer pauses if you switch to another tab or window.</li>
    <li>If you close the page, you continue from the same step next time.</li>
    <li>If your teacher changes your mark later, you are asked to read the feedback again.</li>
    <li>If you never open the feedback, your mark is still released after a waiting period set by your institution.</li>
</ul>
</section>

{{! ----- Messages and penalties ----- }}
<section id="student-messages">
<h3>Messages, late penalties and translation</h3>

<h4>Message your teacher about a piece of work</h4>
<p>The speech-bubble icon on the activity page and on the feedback page opens a message thread
about that piece of work. You can write before and after it is graded, and you are notified when
your teacher replies. On assignments this takes the place of Moodle's own submission comments.</p>

<h4>Late penalties</h4>
<p>If you submit after the due date and the activity applies late penalties, your feedback page
lists the penalty and shows your grade after it. Each day that has started counts as a full day.
If you were given an extension, the penalty is worked out from your extended date.</p>

<h4>Feedback in your language</h4>
<p>On sites that use the translation service for a course, feedback is shown in your language. A
notice appears while a translation is still being prepared.</p>
</section>

</section>
